<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-07-09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Elio Hbeich"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Ontology module for route-specific textile recyclability, assessment criteria and results, barriers, scores and labels, actual recycling events, recovered materials, textile waste categories, recycling yield and recycled-content declarations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/issued> "2026-07-09"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-07-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2026-05/Textiles_DPP_20260513.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-ontology> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "EU DPP Textile Recyclability Ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "txtrec" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability#" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Recyclability is represented as route-specific potential assessed under stated collection, sorting, preparation and recycling conditions. It must not be inferred from a universal boolean."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Recycled content is represented separately from recyclability: a product can contain recycled material without being recyclable through a given route, and a recyclable product may contain no recycled material."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Scores and labels are method-specific and do not constitute adopted regulatory classifications unless a future delegated act or standard defines them."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "EU DPP Textile Recyclability Ontology"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "Version 1.1.2" .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "CIRPASS Textile Ontology modelling specification, version 1.1.0."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-recyclability> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceType> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#projectDecision> .
